P(id='M2', sec='M', title='Research methods for an ongoing study', stage='evergreen', stamp='METHOD', date='2026-11-11',
  cues=['Why a living review?', 'How do we rate evidence?', 'How do we test models honestly?'],
  body=[{'t':'ul','items':['**Living review**: a review \u201ccontinually updated, incorporating relevant new evidence as it becomes available\u201d [@W:lsr]. The motive is stark: the median time from a study\u2019s publication to its inclusion in a systematic review has been 2.5 to 6.5 years [@W:lsrcochrane].','**Living guidelines** update an individual recommendation, not the whole guideline [@W:livingguide]. Here, the unit of update is the note.','**GRADE**-style certainty: four levels (high, moderate, low, very low), rated down for risk of bias, inconsistency, indirectness, imprecision and publication bias [@W:gradebmj] [@W:gradepmc].','**Walk-forward evaluation**: every model is scored only on matches it could not have seen, the way it would run live ([[G4]]).']}],
  stickies=[{'c':'green','x':'Cadence: monthly searches, dated entries, old conclusions struck through, never deleted.'}],
  summary='Borrow medicine\u2019s best evidence habits: keep it living, rate it honestly, and test it the way it will be used.', links=['M3','G4','M0'])
